    21	#    - The scene stays the same: an 11x11 grid, a fixed 3x3 green destination around one red center,
    22	#      orange floor, optional magenta walls, and scattered maroon tokens.
    23	#    - Connectivity still comes from flood-fill through floor/maroon cells starting at passable cells
    24	#      adjacent to the destination.
    25	#    - The changed step is only the ranking of reachable maroons. In the original task, if reachable
    26	#      maroons were at (1,8),(2,2),(8,1),(9,9) with distances 1,5,3,2, the chosen order was by
    27	#      (distance,row,col): (1,8),(9,9),(8,1),(2,2). In this variant the chosen order is by
    28	#      (row,col): (1,8),(2,2),(8,1),(9,9). The destination still fills in its own row-major order.
    29	# b) Complexity calibration:
    30	#    - If the number of reachable maroons is <= 9, every reachable maroon moves and the new ranking
    31	#      becomes invisible. To make D3 observable, the generator intentionally creates 10-14 reachable
    32	#      maroons, so only 9 move and some remain behind.
    33	#    - The generator also rejects samples where distance-order and scan-order happen to pick the same
    34	#      9 sources; otherwise the instance would collapse back to the original behavior.
    35	# c) Implicit assumption audit on the original solver:
    36	#    - Destination detection by the unique red center is still valid.
    37	#    - Floor-color inference from the ring around the destination still assumes at least one adjacent
    38	#      non-maroon non-destination cell remains visible. The generator therefore reserves at least one
    39	#      floor opening next to the destination.
    40	#    - BFS reachability through {floor, maroon} remains valid because D3 changes only ranking, not
    41	#      eligibility.
    42	#    - The original `maroons.sort()` encoded the old dimension directly. That line must change to sort
    43	#      by coordinates only after reachability has been determined.
    44	# d) Placement legality:
    45	#    - Source maroons are sampled only from reachable floor cells outside the 3x3 destination.
    46	#    - Distractors are sampled only from unreachable floor cells, so they never overlap walls,
    47	#      destination cells, or source maroons.
    48	#    - The reserved adjacent floor cell guarantees both in-bounds placement and solver compatibility.
    49	# e) Visual observability:
    50	#    - The changed ordering is based only on visible positions, never on hidden ids or generation-time
    51	#      metadata.
    52	#    - With >9 reachable maroons, the output shows a full 3x3 maroon block plus leftover maroons whose
    53	#      positions differ from the old distance-based task, making the variant inferable from examples.
    54	# f) Visual cleanliness:
    55	#    - The destination region remains a simple fixed landmark.
    56	#    - Walls still separate reachable from unreachable zones, so moved vs unmoved maroons are spatially
    57	#      legible rather than mixed inside one cluttered area.
    58	# g) Color inference:
    59	#    - No new color mapping is introduced. The only colors stay red/green/orange/magenta/maroon.
    60	#    - Sorting depends on row-major spatial order, which is directly readable from the grid.
    61	# h) Generator validation strategy:
    62	#    - Build a candidate input, run the new solver, run a private old-style distance-ranked solver,
    63	#      and accept the input only if both succeed and produce different outputs.
    64	# i) New main() assumptions and generator guarantees:
    65	#    - main() assumes exactly one red center, at least one passable neighbor of the destination, and at
    66	#      least one visible floor-colored ring cell for floor inference.
    67	#    - generate_input() guarantees these conditions by construction and rejects candidates that do not.
    68	
    69	
    70	# ---- CFG: tunable generation parameters ----
    71	GRID_H, GRID_W = 11, 11
    72	CENTER_R, CENTER_C = 5, 5
    73	FLOOR_COLOR, WALL_COLOR = 7, 6
    74	DEST_COLOR, RED_CENTER = 3, 2
    75	MAROON = 9
    76	
    77	WALL_PROB = 0.75
    78	RING_GAP_RANGE = (1, 4)
    79	WALL_STYLES = ["arms", "frame", "mixed"]
    80	
    81	ARM_EXTEND_PROB = 0.5
    82	ARM_LENGTH_RANGE = (1, 5)
    83	FRAME_DIST_RANGE = (3, 4)
    84	FRAME_CONNECT_PROB = 0.4
    85	FRAME_GAP_REMOVE_PROB = 0.3
    86	MIXED_EXTEND_PROB = 0.6
    87	
    88	REACHABLE_MAROON_RANGE = (10, 14)
    89	DISTRACTOR_MAX = 6
    90	TOTAL_MAROON_RANGE = (10, 16)
    91	MIN_REACHABLE_FLOOR = REACHABLE_MAROON_RANGE[0] + 1
    92	GEN_RETRIES = 400
    93	SOURCE_SAMPLE_RETRIES = 80
    94	INF = 10**9
